   "subject": "Re: [r-inla] different priors for GLM",
   "parts": [
    [
     1,
     "<div dir=\"ltr\"><div>Hi Virgilio,</div><div><br></div><div>I recap what I wrote before:</div><div><br></div><div>the priors I would put on intercept is a Cauchy(0,10) and a t-student (0,0.03) with 1 degree of freedom for the coefficients of the covariates.</div><div><br></div>I try doing:<div><br></div><div>inla_model &lt;- inla (y ~ f(1,model=&#39;linear&#39;,, ) + f(AGE,model=&#39;linear&#39;) + f(CLASS,model=&#39;linear&#39;)+ f(INCOME, model=&#39;linear) -1 , \r\n\r\ndata=df, family=&#39;binomial&#39; )</div><div><br></div><div>but where do I have to explicit the priors (and their parameters in the f()  supposing to fix location=0 and scale=10 aand the same procedure for t-student)? :(</div><div><br></div><div><br></div><div><br></div><div>                       <br></div></div>"
    ],
    [
     3,
     "<br><div class=\"gmail_quote\"><div dir=\"ltr\" class=\"gmail_attr\">Il giorno gio 14 mag 2020 alle ore 18:21 Virgilio Gómez-Rubio &lt;<a href data-email-masked rel=\"nofollow\">becario...@gmail.com</a>&gt; ha scritto:<br></div><blockquote class=\"gmail_quote\" style=\"margin:0px 0px 0px 0.8ex;border-left:1px solid rgb(204,204,204);padding-left:1ex\"><div><div dir=\"auto\"><div dir=\"auto\">Hi,<div><br></div><div><br></div><div><div><blockquote type=\"cite\"><div><div dir=\"ltr\"><div>I&#39;m quite confused when facing up with random and fixed effect on the priors. How can I explicit separate priors for intercept and coefficient of the covariates?</div></div></div></blockquote><div><br></div><div><div>First of all, you can check ?INLA::control.fixed to see how the prior mean and precision of the intercept and fixed effects are defined.</div><div><br></div><div>You can also use the latent effect ‘linear’ [1] to define a fixed effect in the linear predictor using the ‘f’-function. This way you can choose the prior on the coefficient to be other than Gausssian. For the intercept you could use a covariate with values equal to 1 and the ‘liner’ latent effect, but remember to remove the default intercept in the linear predictor.</div><div><br></div></div><br><blockquote type=\"cite\"><div><div dir=\"ltr\"><div>I did:</div><div><br></div><div><pre style=\"padding:0.85em 1em;border-width:initial;border-style:none;box-sizing:border-box;font-family:Consolas,&quot;Liberation Mono&quot;,Menlo,Courier,monospace;font-size:16px;white-space:pre-wrap;break-inside:avoid;direction:ltr;color:rgb(51,51,51);overflow:auto;background:rgb(247,247,247);letter-spacing:0.2px\"><span style=\"color:inherit;text-decoration-line:inherit;background-color:initial;font-size:0.85em;white-space:pre-wrap;letter-spacing:0.2px\">HT.prior =</span><span style=\"text-decoration-line:inherit;background-color:initial;font-size:0.85em;white-space:pre-wrap;letter-spacing:0.2px;box-sizing:border-box;color:rgb(64,112,160)\"> &quot;expression:</span><br></pre></div><div><pre style=\"box-sizing:border-box;font-family:Consolas,&quot;Liberation Mono&quot;,Menlo,Courier,monospace;font-size:16px;white-space:pre-wrap;break-inside:avoid;direction:ltr;border-width:initial;border-style:none;color:rgb(51,51,51);overflow:auto;padding:0.85em 1em;background:rgb(247,247,247);letter-spacing:0.2px\"><code style=\"box-sizing:border-box;font-family:Consolas,&quot;Liberation Mono&quot;,Menlo,Courier,monospace;font-size:0.85em;white-space:pre-wrap;break-inside:avoid;direction:ltr;border-width:initial;border-style:none;color:inherit;background:0px 0px;display:inline;max-width:initial;overflow:initial;line-height:inherit\"><span style=\"box-sizing:border-box;color:inherit;text-decoration:inherit;display:inline-block;line-height:1.25\"><a href=\"https://becarioprecario.bitbucket.io/inla-gitbook/ch-priors.html#cb181-2\" style=\"box-sizing:border-box;color:rgb(65,131,196);background:0px 0px\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"nofollow\" data-saferedirecturl=\"https://www.google.com/url?hl=en-US&amp;q=https://becarioprecario.bitbucket.io/inla-gitbook/ch-priors.html%23cb181-2&amp;source=gmail&amp;ust=1792440935477000&amp;usg=AOvVaw0YhuT4GJUjaMCsQAbZOen4\"></a><span style=\"box-sizing:border-box;color:rgb(64,112,160)\">  sigma = exp(-theta/2);</span></span>\r\n<span style=\"box-sizing:border-box;color:inherit;text-decoration:inherit;display:inline-block;line-height:1.25\"><a href=\"https://becarioprecario.bitbucket.io/inla-gitbook/ch-priors.html#cb181-3\" style=\"box-sizing:border-box;color:rgb(65,131,196);background:0px 0px\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"nofollow\" data-saferedirecturl=\"https://www.google.com/url?hl=en-US&amp;q=https://becarioprecario.bitbucket.io/inla-gitbook/ch-priors.html%23cb181-3&amp;source=gmail&amp;ust=1792440935477000&amp;usg=AOvVaw19mLWAs-L7w0LD1jpAUFtM\"></a><span style=\"box-sizing:border-box;color:rgb(64,112,160)\">  nu = 3;</span></span>\r\n<span style=\"box-sizing:border-box;color:inherit;text-decoration:inherit;display:inline-block;line-height:1.25\"><a href=\"https://becarioprecario.bitbucket.io/inla-gitbook/ch-priors.html#cb181-4\" style=\"box-sizing:border-box;color:rgb(65,131,196);background:0px 0px\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"nofollow\" data-saferedirecturl=\"https://www.google.com/url?hl=en-US&amp;q=https://becarioprecario.bitbucket.io/inla-gitbook/ch-priors.html%23cb181-4&amp;source=gmail&amp;ust=1792440935477000&amp;usg=AOvVaw3wvQp6MgGIZ6oMMEMCU3X1\"></a><span style=\"box-sizing:border-box;color:rgb(64,112,160)\">  log_dens = 0 - 0.5 * log(nu * pi) - (-0.1207822);</span></span>\r\n<span style=\"box-sizing:border-box;color:inherit;text-decoration:inherit;display:inline-block;line-height:1.25\"><a href=\"https://becarioprecario.bitbucket.io/inla-gitbook/ch-priors.html#cb181-5\" style=\"box-sizing:border-box;color:rgb(65,131,196);background:0px 0px\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"nofollow\" data-saferedirecturl=\"https://www.google.com/url?hl=en-US&amp;q=https://becarioprecario.bitbucket.io/inla-gitbook/ch-priors.html%23cb181-5&amp;source=gmail&amp;ust=1792440935477000&amp;usg=AOvVaw3iCAV7m6ulofauq-7t4VCd\"></a><span style=\"box-sizing:border-box;color:rgb(64,112,160)\">  log_dens = log_dens - 0.5 * (nu + 1) * log(1 + sigma * sigma);</span></span>\r\n<span style=\"box-sizing:border-box;color:inherit;text-decoration:inherit;display:inline-block;line-height:1.25\"><a href=\"https://becarioprecario.bitbucket.io/inla-gitbook/ch-priors.html#cb181-6\" style=\"box-sizing:border-box;color:rgb(65,131,196);background:0px 0px\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"nofollow\" data-saferedirecturl=\"https://www.google.com/url?hl=en-US&amp;q=https://becarioprecario.bitbucket.io/inla-gitbook/ch-priors.html%23cb181-6&amp;source=gmail&amp;ust=1792440935477000&amp;usg=AOvVaw1nDURye6QsvG_hguBguRkN\"></a><span style=\"box-sizing:border-box;color:rgb(64,112,160)\">  log_dens = log_dens - log(2) - theta / 2;</span></span>\r\n<span style=\"box-sizing:border-box;color:inherit;text-decoration:inherit;display:inline-block;line-height:1.25\"><a href=\"https://becarioprecario.bitbucket.io/inla-gitbook/ch-priors.html#cb181-7\" style=\"box-sizing:border-box;color:rgb(65,131,196);background:0px 0px\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"nofollow\" data-saferedirecturl=\"https://www.google.com/url?hl=en-US&amp;q=https://becarioprecario.bitbucket.io/inla-gitbook/ch-priors.html%23cb181-7&amp;source=gmail&amp;ust=1792440935477000&amp;usg=AOvVaw2WXWH7OqfQ7EzkPXqbf0UB\"></a><span style=\"box-sizing:border-box;color:rgb(64,112,160)\">  return(log_dens);</span></span>\r\n<span style=\"box-sizing:border-box;color:inherit;text-decoration:inherit;display:inline-block;line-height:1.25\"><a href=\"https://becarioprecario.bitbucket.io/inla-gitbook/ch-priors.html#cb181-8\" style=\"box-sizing:border-box;color:rgb(65,131,196);background:0px 0px\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"nofollow\" data-saferedirecturl=\"https://www.google.com/url?hl=en-US&amp;q=https://becarioprecario.bitbucket.io/inla-gitbook/ch-priors.html%23cb181-8&amp;source=gmail&amp;ust=1792440935477000&amp;usg=AOvVaw1FtNatRyr49NTkAkTpXiJe\"></a><span style=\"box-sizing:border-box;color:rgb(64,112,160)\">&quot;</span></span></code></pre></div><div><br></div><div>inla_model &lt;- inla ( Y ~ AGE + CLASS + INCOME , data=df, family=&#39;binomial&#39;,control_family=list=(hyper=<span style=\"color:inherit;text-decoration-line:inherit;background-color:initial;font-family:Consolas,&quot;Liberation Mono&quot;,Menlo,Courier,monospace;font-size:0.85em;white-space:pre-wrap;letter-spacing:0.2px\">HT.prior</span>)).</div><div><br></div><div>But It doesn&#39;t work.. where do I have to put prior on intercept and coefficients of covariates?</div></div></div></blockquote><div><br></div><div>This is a prior on the precision to have a half-T prior on the standard deviation [2]. BTW, I spotted some typos in the name of the half-catchy and half-t priors. It should be HT and not HN as this is for the half-normal.</div><div><br></div><div>In your code, I believe that you must use something like</div><div><br></div><div>control.family = list(hyper = list(prec = HT.prior)))</div><div><br></div><div><br></div><div>Best,</div><div><br></div><div>Virgilio</div></div><br></div><div><br></div><div>[1] <a href=\"https://becarioprecario.bitbucket.io/inla-gitbook/ch-mixed.html#linear-fixed-effect\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"nofollow\" data-saferedirecturl=\"https://www.google.com/url?hl=en-US&amp;q=https://becarioprecario.bitbucket.io/inla-gitbook/ch-mixed.html%23linear-fixed-effect&amp;source=gmail&amp;ust=1792440935477000&amp;usg=AOvVaw1ppJ4doKGHTKK-FOgY54Tm\">https://becarioprecario.bitbucket.io/inla-gitbook/ch-mixed.html#linear-fixed-effect</a></div><div><br></div><div>[2] <a href=\"https://becarioprecario.bitbucket.io/inla-gitbook/ch-priors.html#example\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"nofollow\" data-saferedirecturl=\"https://www.google.com/url?hl=en-US&amp;q=https://becarioprecario.bitbucket.io/inla-gitbook/ch-priors.html%23example&amp;source=gmail&amp;ust=1792440935477000&amp;usg=AOvVaw1mXhUtzXqItfd1xp5nve5y\">https://becarioprecario.bitbucket.io/inla-gitbook/ch-priors.html#example</a></div><div><br></div></div></div></div></blockquote></div>\r\n"
    ]
